{% comment %}
  One ASCII backdrop. Reads a generated field from _data/ascii/ and stacks its
  layers back to front over a faint plate of the source painting, so the reader
  can make out what the characters are describing.

  Params:
    field    key under site.data.ascii (default: bosch_field)
    variant  "wide" (default) or "compact"
    hidden   render it hidden, for an alternate the picker may reveal instead

  Called once per variant: a landscape composition for wide viewports and a
  portrait one for phones, swapped by media query in _sass/_atelier-hero.scss.
  Only the wide variant carries data-ascii-field, because that is what the motion
  script drives and the script is inert at phone sizes anyway.

  Each row is its own element rather than one run of text: the pointer effect
  displaces rows individually, and explicit row heights keep the layers in
  register whatever their content. The container stays a <pre> because the HTML
  minifier collapses runs of spaces everywhere else, which would scramble the
  composition; the rows are emitted back to back so no stray whitespace between
  them is rendered as a line.

  The artwork is decorative, so the whole field is hidden from assistive tech and
  from the pointer. It is real text, escaped at render time, so any character in
  the source data is safe to use.
{% endcomment %}

{% capture ascii_newline %}
{% endcapture %}

{% assign field_key = include.field %}
{% if field_key == blank or field_key == true %}
  {% assign field_key = 'bosch_field' %}
{% endif %}
{% assign field = site.data.ascii[field_key] %}
{% assign variant = include.variant | default: 'wide' %}

{% if field %}
  {% assign hero_rows = field.hero_rows | default: field.rows %}
  {% capture ascii_metrics %}--ascii-columns: {{ field.columns }}; --ascii-rows: {{ field.rows }}; --ascii-hero-rows: {{ hero_rows }}{% endcapture %}
  <div
    class="ascii-field ascii-field--{{ variant }}"
    {% if variant == 'wide' %}
      data-ascii-field
    {% endif %}
    {% if include.alternate %}
      data-ascii-alt
    {% endif %}
    {% if include.hidden %}
      hidden
    {% endif %}
    aria-hidden="true"
    role="presentation"
  >
    {% if field.plate.url %}
      <img
        class="ascii-field__plate"
        data-ascii-plate
        src="{{ field.plate.url | relative_url }}"
        width="{{ field.plate.width }}"
        height="{{ field.plate.height }}"
        alt=""
        loading="lazy"
        decoding="async"
        style="{{ ascii_metrics }}"
      >
    {% endif %}

    {% for layer in field.layers %}
      {%- assign ascii_rows = layer.art | split: ascii_newline -%}
      <pre
        class="ascii-field__layer ascii-field__layer--{{ layer.id }}"
        data-ascii-layer="{{ layer.id }}"
        data-depth="{{ forloop.index }}"
        style="{{ ascii_metrics }}"
      >{% for row in ascii_rows %}<span>{{ row | escape }}</span>{% endfor %}</pre>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
{% endif %}
